planted_hunks: settings.html @@ -15,17 +15,14 @@ (re-wraps the General section in its own submit-button-less form); @@ -36,49 +33,49 @@ (strips the form="settings-form" association attributes from the General inputs); @@ -90,7 +87,7 @@ and @@ -134,10 +131,7 @@ (form-boundary restructuring)

## What the reversed patch re-introduces
The fix (542d5dd) associated the General settings fields with the instances form
via the HTML `form="settings-form"` attribute (Security stays a separate form since
nested forms are illegal HTML). The reversed patch (this .patch =
`git diff 542d5dd 542d5dd^ -- triggarr/templates/settings.html`) re-splits the
General section into its own `<form action=save_settings>` with NO submit button,
while the 'Save Settings' button sits in a separate form holding only the instance
fields: clicking Save submits only the instances form, so every General field
(skip_unreleased, log_level, counts, etc.) is ABSENT from the POST and silently
reset to its form-default on each save. Silent data-loss-on-save; the page renders
and "saves" without error — the reviewer must notice the form-association break.

